00:19:10.785 --> 00:19:13.049
- Thank you. Hi, thank God.
- How can l help you?


00:19:13.087 --> 00:19:16.989
l'm Mary Walsh. My boyfriend
had surgery here this morning.


00:19:17.024 --> 00:19:18.753
- He's missing.
- Missing?


00:19:18.793 --> 00:19:21.227
- Yes.
- l told her there was no one


00:19:21.262 --> 00:19:23.730
who's checked into this hospital
by the name of Kevin Peterson.


00:19:23.764 --> 00:19:26.597
Okay, well, he had
orthopedic surgery--


00:19:26.634 --> 00:19:29.194
A.C.L.-- this morning.


00:19:29.236 --> 00:19:30.726
His doctor
is Dr. Harding.


00:19:30.771 --> 00:19:33.740
Evidently, neither one
of them are in your system.


00:19:33.774 --> 00:19:37.141
And no one's in his room.


00:19:37.178 --> 00:19:39.271
Okay, well, obviously there's been
some kind of mistake.


00:19:39.313 --> 00:19:41.281
That's what l've been trying
to explain to you.


00:19:41.315 --> 00:19:44.113
Come with me, please.
Let me see what we can do.


00:19:44.151 --> 00:19:47.120
What time this morning was it that you
and your boyfriend arrived?


00:19:47.154 --> 00:19:49.987
About 7:15.
Surgery started at 8:00.


00:19:50.024 --> 00:19:52.185
Okay, and you're the one


00:19:52.226 --> 00:19:54.854
- who arrived here with him.
- Correct.


00:19:56.664 --> 00:19:59.929
Okay.


00:19:59.967 --> 00:20:02.868
Oh...
Rewind that a hair.


00:20:06.874 --> 00:20:09.342
Wait, stop.


00:20:09.376 --> 00:20:11.606
All right,
these numbers don't--


00:20:11.645 --> 00:20:13.670
These times don't coincide.


00:20:13.714 --> 00:20:15.545
Keep fast-forwarding,
please.


00:20:15.583 --> 00:20:19.349
We weren't even out
of bed yet.


00:20:19.386 --> 00:20:22.219
Okay, keep going.


00:20:22.256 --> 00:20:25.020
( sighs )


00:20:29.163 --> 00:20:31.791
Okay, right here.


00:20:31.832 --> 00:20:33.993
We were already here.


00:20:34.034 --> 00:20:36.662
Back it up, please.


00:20:36.704 --> 00:20:39.195
Okay, now...


00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:41.902
rewind it just a hair.


00:20:44.411 --> 00:20:45.878
Wait, wait.


00:20:45.913 --> 00:20:47.881
Wait, did you see that?


00:20:47.915 --> 00:20:50.076
Turn it back.


00:20:50.117 --> 00:20:53.086
Go back a bit.
Play it from this point.


00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.246
Good.


00:21:03.531 --> 00:21:06.557
Keep playing, please.


00:21:10.871 --> 00:21:13.669
Pause! That's him.


00:21:13.707 --> 00:21:15.174
Right there.


00:21:15.209 --> 00:21:17.336
That's him.


00:21:17.378 --> 00:21:19.403
He's wearing the green
and gray striped shirt.


00:21:19.446 --> 00:21:22.882
Color accuracy is difficult to determine
on closed-circuit cameras.


00:21:22.917 --> 00:21:25.750
You've gotta be kidding me.
That's him. He's right there.


00:21:25.786 --> 00:21:28.812
Markham: Miss Walsh.


00:21:28.856 --> 00:21:31.620
Mary:
l'm looking at him, you know?


00:21:33.761 --> 00:21:37.424
He may not be in your computer,
but he's right on your security camera.


00:21:37.464 --> 00:21:40.456
Do you have a copy of his hospital
appointment record?


00:21:40.501 --> 00:21:43.299
No, it was on him.


00:21:46.807 --> 00:21:49.742
( sighs )
Oh God.


00:21:49.777 --> 00:21:53.042
lt might be in his
computer bag in the car.


00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:55.275
l will have my team
look for him,


00:21:55.316 --> 00:21:59.275
- but you know l'm understaffed.
- Yeah.


00:21:59.320 --> 00:22:00.810
Where do you think
you're going?


00:22:00.854 --> 00:22:04.517
l'm gonna go call somebody who
can actually help me out here.


00:22:12.399 --> 00:22:14.367
l just didn't think there was
anything conclusive on that.


00:22:14.401 --> 00:22:17.097
Do what you can,
but...


00:22:17.137 --> 00:22:18.934
- You got it, Miss Markham.
- Thank you.


00:22:18.973 --> 00:22:22.101
- ( static )
- Yeah, come in.


00:22:23.577 --> 00:22:25.408
- Man: Breathe in...
- ( breathing )


00:22:25.446 --> 00:22:28.279
...out, in...


00:22:28.315 --> 00:22:30.180
out.


00:22:33.153 --> 00:22:36.782
- How is it, Doc?
- lt's 160 over 100.


00:22:36.824 --> 00:22:38.792
You still taking
the medication?


00:22:38.826 --> 00:22:41.659
Every day.


00:22:41.695 --> 00:22:44.186
- What about work?
- What about it?


00:22:44.231 --> 00:22:46.199
l don't know, Rich.


00:22:46.233 --> 00:22:48.201
Something like this
takes time.


00:22:48.235 --> 00:22:49.964
You don't wanna rush it.


00:22:50.004 --> 00:22:52.097
Heaven forbid.


00:22:52.139 --> 00:22:54.505
- l'm gonna increase the dosage though.
- Okay, thanks.


00:22:54.541 --> 00:22:57.704
But l really need you
to take it easy, man.


00:22:57.745 --> 00:23:00.213
Whatever you say, Doc.


00:23:00.247 --> 00:23:02.715
All right.
See you on Thursday?


00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:04.911
- Wouldn't miss it.
- All right, take care.


00:23:14.028 --> 00:23:15.996
- Franklin here.
- Woman: This is dispatch.


00:23:16.030 --> 00:23:19.227
We've got reports of a missing person
at County Memorial.


00:23:19.266 --> 00:23:21.996
- Are you still there?
- Yeah, l'm still here.


00:23:22.036 --> 00:23:24.027
What floor?


00:23:29.109 --> 00:23:31.577
Mary: When l arrived,
he wasn't in his room.


00:23:31.612 --> 00:23:35.571
So l went down
to the waiting room


00:23:35.616 --> 00:23:39.416
and waited there
for a good couple of hours.


00:23:39.453 --> 00:23:41.978
Started getting
increasingly concerned


00:23:42.022 --> 00:23:45.822
and went back to his floor
and spoke with the head nurse


00:23:45.859 --> 00:23:49.090
and learned for the first time
that he was not in the computer system.


00:23:49.129 --> 00:23:52.121
We have looked. No one by the name
of Kevin Peterson was scheduled


00:23:52.166 --> 00:23:54.464
for anything today,
not even a check-up.


00:23:54.501 --> 00:23:57.493
What about the nurse,
this Amanda?


00:23:57.538 --> 00:23:59.403
We don't have anyone
on staff by that name,


00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:02.068
- and the doctor that he was supposedly--
- Dr. Harding.


00:24:02.109 --> 00:24:04.509
scheduled with
is on vacation.


00:24:04.545 --> 00:24:07.378
Look, if you could just access Kevin's
insurance records.


00:24:07.414 --> 00:24:09.405
l'm sorry.
l can't do that.


00:24:09.450 --> 00:24:11.213
Why?


00:24:11.251 --> 00:24:13.446
The insurance company will
only release information


00:24:13.487 --> 00:24:15.455
to the policyholder's
spouse.


00:24:15.489 --> 00:24:19.289
Okay, but this is an emergency situation.
He's missing.


00:24:19.326 --> 00:24:22.454
l'm sorry. The hospital
can't release any information


00:24:22.496 --> 00:24:24.760
to a non-family member
without a court order.


00:24:24.798 --> 00:24:27.266
Detective...


00:24:27.301 --> 00:24:29.792
l'm getting
really really worried


00:24:29.837 --> 00:24:32.135
that something bad's
happened to him.


00:24:34.241 --> 00:24:36.766
Can you please help me?


00:24:36.810 --> 00:24:38.903
Okay, first of all,


00:24:38.946 --> 00:24:41.210
l can't file a report
for 24 hours.


00:24:41.248 --> 00:24:43.307
24 hours?


00:24:43.350 --> 00:24:45.113
l'll be honest with you,
Miss Walsh,


00:24:45.152 --> 00:24:48.053
most of the time we get
a call saying a spouse


00:24:48.088 --> 00:24:51.990
or boyfriend or whatever
is missing,


00:24:52.025 --> 00:24:53.754
usually they just up
and left.


00:24:53.794 --> 00:24:56.422
Have you considered
the possibility


00:24:56.463 --> 00:24:59.489
that your boyfriend
might have walked out on you?


00:24:59.533 --> 00:25:01.899
l could see how you two
would think that,


00:25:01.935 --> 00:25:05.132
but that's just
not him, no.


00:25:05.172 --> 00:25:07.766
- How long have you been together?
- Four months.


00:25:07.808 --> 00:25:10.003
Markham: That's not a lot of time
to get to know someone.


00:25:11.945 --> 00:25:14.641
Maybe your relationship
isn't what you thought it was.


00:25:14.681 --> 00:25:17.650
No, l trust him.


00:25:17.684 --> 00:25:19.811
Detective Franklin:
Do you have a picture?


00:25:21.288 --> 00:25:22.778
Maybe, wait.


00:25:25.626 --> 00:25:28.356
l think.
Hold on, l think l do.


00:25:28.395 --> 00:25:31.626
Yeah, right here.


00:25:34.868 --> 00:25:36.392
Can you make
anything out?


00:25:36.436 --> 00:25:38.597
Markham:
No.


00:25:38.639 --> 00:25:40.470
Well, it's not
the best picture.


00:25:40.507 --> 00:25:43.271
lt's something.


00:25:43.310 --> 00:25:45.073
How about a description?


00:25:45.112 --> 00:25:49.071
He's 6'0'',
maybe 6'1''.


00:25:49.116 --> 00:25:51.846
Around 190.


00:25:51.885 --> 00:25:54.217
Brown hair.


00:25:54.254 --> 00:25:56.279
Brown eyes.


00:25:56.323 --> 00:25:58.917
He was wearing
a green


00:25:58.959 --> 00:26:02.360
and gray shirt today
and shorts


00:26:02.396 --> 00:26:04.887
because he has
on a huge leg brace.


00:26:04.932 --> 00:26:06.524
And he was using a crutch.


00:26:06.567 --> 00:26:09.365
Shirt was
long-sleeved.


00:26:11.438 --> 00:26:13.406
Security has their people
searching the entire hospital


00:26:13.440 --> 00:26:17.399
and no one has seen anyone
matching that description.


00:26:17.444 --> 00:26:19.912
l'll see
what l can find.


00:26:19.947 --> 00:26:21.915
ln the meantime,
l need you to sit right here.


00:26:21.949 --> 00:26:23.644
l feel very awkward


00:26:23.684 --> 00:26:25.652
just not doing anything
and staying here.


00:26:25.686 --> 00:26:27.984
Miss Walsh, the more cooperation
l can get from you,


00:26:28.021 --> 00:26:29.852
the faster this can go
for everyone.


00:26:29.890 --> 00:26:31.517
All right? Okay?


00:26:31.558 --> 00:26:33.822
- Okay.
- Thank you.


00:26:33.861 --> 00:26:34.987
Thank you.


00:26:35.028 --> 00:26:36.996
lf you hear anything,
give me a call.


00:26:37.030 --> 00:26:39.965
- Anything l can do to help.
- Thank you.


00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:41.490
Thank you.


00:26:41.535 --> 00:26:44.868
- l'm sorry.
- Me too.


00:26:44.905 --> 00:26:46.497
Will you excuse me
for a minute?


00:26:46.540 --> 00:26:48.098
Yes, of course.


00:27:06.627 --> 00:27:08.618
- ( bell dings )
- ( sighs )


00:27:11.965 --> 00:27:15.457
Have you seen a male Caucasian,
mid 30s, dark hair,


00:27:15.502 --> 00:27:18.437
wearing dark shorts,
green sweatshirt?


00:27:18.472 --> 00:27:22.340
Excuse me, you wouldn't happen
to recall seeing a male Caucasian mid 30s,


00:27:22.376 --> 00:27:24.936
wearing a gray-striped
hoodie with shorts?


00:27:24.978 --> 00:27:28.106
- No.
- Okay, thank you.


00:27:34.588 --> 00:27:36.988
Could you tell me where
the outpatient surgery is?


00:27:37.024 --> 00:27:38.992
Yeah, if you just keep going
straight down the hall


00:27:39.026 --> 00:27:41.426
you'll run right into it.


00:28:06.219 --> 00:28:08.551
Woman:
Can l help you, sir?


00:28:08.588 --> 00:28:11.887
Yeah, l couldn't help
but notice


00:28:11.925 --> 00:28:14.155
there are no patients
on this level.


00:28:14.194 --> 00:28:16.458
Yeah, everyone's been moved
to another facility.


00:28:16.496 --> 00:28:19.624
They are shutting this entire hospital down
Saturday for renovation.


00:28:19.666 --> 00:28:22.965
You mean no one has been
in any of these rooms today?


00:28:23.003 --> 00:28:25.870
No. Are you looking
for someone?


00:28:25.906 --> 00:28:29.774
( sighs )
l'm fine, thanks.


00:28:29.810 --> 00:28:32.938
You wouldn't happen
to know


00:28:32.980 --> 00:28:35.005
of a nurse named Amanda,
would you?


00:28:35.048 --> 00:28:37.312
Amanda? No.


00:28:37.351 --> 00:28:39.342
- No, no one.
- Are you sure?


00:28:39.386 --> 00:28:41.684
l'm the head nurse.
l would know.


00:28:41.722 --> 00:28:44.350
- Thanks.
- Have a good day.


00:28:44.391 --> 00:28:46.552
Franklin: Excuse me, l'm looking
for a patient by the name


00:28:46.593 --> 00:28:48.959
of Kevin Peterson...


00:28:48.996 --> 00:28:50.156
Excuse me,
l'm looking for a guy,


00:28:50.197 --> 00:28:53.189
mid 30s, 6' tall--
Kevin Peterson.


00:28:53.233 --> 00:28:55.201
He's wearing
a striped hoodie.


00:28:55.235 --> 00:28:56.896
You wouldn't happen to recall
seeing a male Caucasian, mid 30s,


00:28:56.937 --> 00:28:59.497
wearing a gray-striped
hoodie with shorts?


00:28:59.539 --> 00:29:02.406
- Woman: No.
- Kevin Peterson checked in, mid 30s.


00:29:02.442 --> 00:29:04.410
l'm looking for a patient
by the name of Kevin Peterson...


00:29:04.444 --> 00:29:07.709
By the name of Kevin Peterson...
Kevin Peterson, checked in today.


00:29:07.748 --> 00:29:11.081
- Gray-striped hoodie with shorts...
- Woman: No.


00:29:11.118 --> 00:29:13.279
Woman: Look, l just clock in
and l clock out.


00:29:13.320 --> 00:29:16.881
You do not recall hearing the name
Kevin Peterson today? ls that right?


00:29:16.923 --> 00:29:19.016
Woman: No.


00:29:43.617 --> 00:29:45.778
( cell phone rings )


00:29:47.654 --> 00:29:50.384
Mary: Chris, l'm in the security room
at the hospital.


00:29:50.424 --> 00:29:51.857
l took Kevin in
and he's missing.


00:29:51.892 --> 00:29:54.486
Look, slow down, okay?
You're scaring me.


00:29:54.528 --> 00:29:57.224
What's going on?
Nobody just disappears.


00:29:57.264 --> 00:29:59.198
No, he is missing.


00:29:59.232 --> 00:30:02.224
l haven't seen him since the surgery.
l feel like l'm going crazy.


00:30:02.269 --> 00:30:03.998
What are you
talking about?


00:30:04.037 --> 00:30:07.370
Saw him in pre-op. Boom,
went back to the room, gone.


00:30:07.407 --> 00:30:10.035
He's not even in the computer system.
He's missing.


00:30:10.077 --> 00:30:13.274
Okay, sweetie, you know,
you just met Kevin.


00:30:13.313 --> 00:30:15.474
Maybe...


00:30:15.515 --> 00:30:17.881
He didn't leave me,
honey.


00:30:17.918 --> 00:30:20.148
Oh my God, sweetheart.
l'm not saying that he left you.


00:30:20.187 --> 00:30:23.213
l know we've only been
together for four months,


00:30:23.256 --> 00:30:25.656
but l have been waiting for him
my whole entire life.


00:30:25.692 --> 00:30:29.321
And l'm not gonna let someone
take him away from me.


00:30:29.362 --> 00:30:32.092
Okay, do you want me to come there?
What do you want me to do?


00:30:32.132 --> 00:30:34.430
Do you want me to call the police?
You're scaring me.


00:30:34.468 --> 00:30:37.767
No, l already called the police.
That's why the detective's here.


00:30:37.804 --> 00:30:39.601
l think l hear
somebody coming.


00:30:39.639 --> 00:30:41.607
( whispering )
Everybody's acting really strange.


00:30:41.641 --> 00:30:43.734
There's something
real off here.


00:30:43.777 --> 00:30:47.611
l think they're all crazy.
Or l'm the crazy one.


00:30:47.647 --> 00:30:50.582
So please, please,
just keep checking in.


00:30:50.617 --> 00:30:53.085
lf l don't answer,
come find me, okay?


00:30:53.120 --> 00:30:55.645
( click )


00:31:09.169 --> 00:31:12.434
l'm having the hardest time
writing on this.


00:31:12.472 --> 00:31:14.167
Oh, here, lean on this.


00:31:14.207 --> 00:31:16.368
Ahh. Thank you.


00:31:33.160 --> 00:31:35.628
- So what's going on?
- What's going on? Well, Miss Walsh,


00:31:35.695 --> 00:31:38.960
Detective Franklin is out
looking for your boyfriend.


00:31:38.999 --> 00:31:41.399
lt's been over an hour.


00:31:41.434 --> 00:31:43.629
lt's a big hospital.


00:31:43.670 --> 00:31:46.298
You know, l think
l'm gonna look myself.


00:31:46.339 --> 00:31:48.307
Listen, l can't
have you doing that.


00:31:48.341 --> 00:31:50.400
l can't have you walking around
the hallway scaring other patients.


00:31:50.443 --> 00:31:53.139
- Do you understand?
- ( Franklin sighs )


00:31:53.180 --> 00:31:55.740
- Hi.
- l've been to all seven floors


00:31:55.782 --> 00:31:58.080
and not a single person
has seen him.


00:31:58.118 --> 00:32:00.780
Okay, um...


00:32:02.656 --> 00:32:06.251
( sighs ) Then please,
l have to file a report.


00:32:06.293 --> 00:32:09.524
l told you he needs to be
missing for 24 hours.


00:32:09.563 --> 00:32:13.397
24 hours is too long.
Anything can happen in 24 hours.


00:32:13.433 --> 00:32:15.663
Please, file a report.


00:32:15.702 --> 00:32:18.170
What does Kevin do
for a living?


00:32:18.205 --> 00:32:21.606
He's in insurance.


00:32:21.641 --> 00:32:24.007
Well, at least
he's covered.


00:32:24.044 --> 00:32:27.070
Have you ever been to his office?
Meet any of his colleagues?


00:32:27.113 --> 00:32:30.105
No, he's freelance.
He works from the house.


00:32:30.150 --> 00:32:34.086
But l did,
while you were gone,


00:32:34.120 --> 00:32:36.816
jot this down for you.


00:32:40.694 --> 00:32:42.525
Wait, you just happened
to remember it?


00:32:42.562 --> 00:32:46.259
l'd appreciate it
if you ran it.


00:32:46.299 --> 00:32:49.097
l'll see
what l can do.


00:32:49.135 --> 00:32:52.866
ln the meantime, is there anybody
else l could talk to?


00:32:52.906 --> 00:32:55.670
Anybody who knew
he'd be here today?


00:32:55.709 --> 00:32:58.701
- What about family?
- Ooh! His mother.


00:32:58.745 --> 00:33:01.441
She lives in Florida,


00:33:01.481 --> 00:33:04.814
but he was gonna put her number
into my phone in case of an emergency.


00:33:04.851 --> 00:33:08.150
l just totally forgot.


00:33:08.188 --> 00:33:10.088
Thank you.


00:33:10.123 --> 00:33:12.990
Okay.


00:33:13.026 --> 00:33:16.018
- ( rings )
- Wait.


00:33:18.064 --> 00:33:21.659
The number you have reached
is not in service at this time.


00:33:21.701 --> 00:33:23.566
- There is no new number.
- No luck.


00:33:23.603 --> 00:33:27.039
He must have input
a wrong digit.


00:33:27.073 --> 00:33:29.598
He's always been bad
electronically.


00:33:35.015 --> 00:33:36.846
Shoot!


00:33:36.883 --> 00:33:40.410
You need proof.
You need some sort of evidence


00:33:40.453 --> 00:33:43.752
that this is real,
that he actually exists,


00:33:43.790 --> 00:33:45.485
don't you?


00:33:48.662 --> 00:33:51.688
- Antidepressants.
- l, uh--


00:33:51.731 --> 00:33:54.461
l have a prescription
for that, so...


00:33:54.501 --> 00:33:57.231
Holloway: That kind of
says it all, doesn't it?


00:33:57.270 --> 00:33:59.363
Please hand that to me.


00:34:01.041 --> 00:34:03.839
l'll be right back,
Mr. Holloway.


00:34:03.877 --> 00:34:06.004
Where are you going?


00:34:07.947 --> 00:34:10.780
May l have
my medication back, please?


00:34:18.325 --> 00:34:20.316
Detective Franklin,


00:34:20.360 --> 00:34:22.692
we have people here
she can talk to.


00:34:22.729 --> 00:34:25.323
l'm sure Miss Markham
could arrange something.


00:34:27.267 --> 00:34:30.031
All right, l'll run
the Social. l'll be back.


00:34:30.070 --> 00:34:33.597
You got it.


00:34:47.520 --> 00:34:49.579
Come on.


00:35:21.721 --> 00:35:23.416
- Wait wait.
- Just stay out of the way.


00:35:23.456 --> 00:35:26.357
Come on.
Your brace.


00:35:26.393 --> 00:35:28.361
Do you want your bag?


00:35:28.395 --> 00:35:30.386
No, just leave it
in the back. That's fine.


00:35:48.848 --> 00:35:50.839
Thank God.


00:36:01.428 --> 00:36:03.419
Where is it?


00:36:06.199 --> 00:36:08.895
Okay, wanna come
upstairs now?


00:36:08.935 --> 00:36:10.926
Shoot!


00:36:14.607 --> 00:36:17.599
Holloway:
lt's not under the seat.


00:36:17.644 --> 00:36:19.373
Shoot!


00:36:20.713 --> 00:36:22.977
Wanna come upstairs now?


00:36:23.016 --> 00:36:25.746
- lt's not here.
- What's not here?


00:36:25.785 --> 00:36:28.185
His bag. lt has
his computer in it,


00:36:28.221 --> 00:36:31.622
all of his information--
everything.


00:36:31.658 --> 00:36:33.888
Somebody had to have
gotten into the car.


00:36:33.927 --> 00:36:36.157
What makes you think that?


00:36:36.196 --> 00:36:38.926
Because the bag was here
this morning. Now it's not.


00:36:38.965 --> 00:36:42.162
- lt was right there.
- Miss Walsh, we need to speak with you.


00:36:42.202 --> 00:36:43.794
Now.


00:36:43.837 --> 00:36:45.998
l have the only set of keys.


00:36:46.039 --> 00:36:48.507
Now.


00:36:57.083 --> 00:36:59.950
We're in the middle
of a huge transition.


00:36:59.986 --> 00:37:02.750
l've got patients to move,
equipment to transport.


00:37:02.789 --> 00:37:05.257
Every minute that l
or my security team


00:37:05.291 --> 00:37:08.226
spends chasing phantoms
on surveillance cameras


00:37:08.261 --> 00:37:11.162
or finding you trespassing
in a restricted area is one less minute


00:37:11.197 --> 00:37:13.165
we're able to do our jobs.


00:37:13.199 --> 00:37:16.066
Every minute you don't spending
looking for Kevin is a minute wasted.


00:37:16.102 --> 00:37:19.162
Mary, l checked seven
floors of this building.


00:37:19.205 --> 00:37:21.469
l checked with every
nurse's station.


00:37:21.508 --> 00:37:24.477
l checked the emergency room.
l checked the intensive care ward.


00:37:24.511 --> 00:37:26.570
What about the wing
that's being renovated?


00:37:26.613 --> 00:37:28.478
Franklin: Yes.


00:37:28.515 --> 00:37:30.915
- And?
- And no one


00:37:30.950 --> 00:37:32.747
reported seeing
your boyfriend.


00:37:32.785 --> 00:37:35.686
No one can even confirm that
he was in this hospital.


00:37:35.722 --> 00:37:37.917
Just what do you suppose
happened to him?


00:37:37.957 --> 00:37:40.152
- l don't know.
- Holloway: Look, there are 23 exits


00:37:40.193 --> 00:37:43.629
in this facility.
Six are manned by my men.


00:37:43.663 --> 00:37:46.564
Eight are alarmed and the rest are
carefully monitored by cameras.


00:37:46.599 --> 00:37:48.829
lf anyone left this building


00:37:48.868 --> 00:37:50.699
under any manner
of duress


00:37:50.737 --> 00:37:52.466
we would know about it.


00:37:52.505 --> 00:37:55.167
Well, obviously, you're not
looking hard enough.


00:37:55.208 --> 00:37:57.870
( cell phone rings )


00:37:57.911 --> 00:38:01.369
- Detective...
- Detective Franklin.


00:38:02.715 --> 00:38:05.707
- Detective, who is it?
- Really?


00:38:05.752 --> 00:38:09.381
Okay, thank you.


00:38:09.422 --> 00:38:11.014
What did they say?


00:38:11.057 --> 00:38:14.185
We ran the Social Security number
you gave me.


00:38:14.227 --> 00:38:17.094
Good, okay,
what's the next step?


00:38:17.130 --> 00:38:20.293
lt belongs to a 50-year-old
African-American woman.


00:38:20.333 --> 00:38:23.928
Well, that's obviously
a mistake.


00:38:23.970 --> 00:38:25.301
Not ours.


00:38:25.338 --> 00:38:26.930
l ran the number
you gave us.


00:38:26.973 --> 00:38:30.238
No, that's impossible.


00:38:30.276 --> 00:38:32.244
Okay, run them
again, please?


00:38:32.278 --> 00:38:34.303
Dr. Bensley,
thank you for joining us.


00:38:34.347 --> 00:38:36.315
l'd like to introduce you
to someone.


00:38:36.349 --> 00:38:39.944
- Hello, Mary.
- Hello.


00:38:39.986 --> 00:38:42.955
Markham: Dr. Bensley is our
hospital psychiatrist.


00:38:42.989 --> 00:38:45.082
l don't need
a psychiatrist.


00:38:45.124 --> 00:38:47.092
Did you get the prescription
l sent over?


00:38:47.126 --> 00:38:49.890
l did. Quite a
potent dosage, Mary.


00:38:49.929 --> 00:38:52.727
Would you mind coming
with me for a moment?


00:38:52.765 --> 00:38:54.562
Yes, actually, l would.


00:38:54.601 --> 00:38:58.230
lt doesn't need to be
voluntary, Miss Walsh.


00:38:58.271 --> 00:39:01.206
Excuse me.
Excuse me!


00:39:01.240 --> 00:39:03.299
Right this way, please.


00:39:03.343 --> 00:39:05.743
This way.


00:39:05.778 --> 00:39:08.508
- Okay.
- Come on.


00:39:22.195 --> 00:39:25.961
So you've been treated for psychiatric
issues before, hmm, Mary?


00:39:28.434 --> 00:39:30.868
Answer the question,
Miss Walsh.


00:39:31.004 --> 00:39:32.938
l...


00:39:34.474 --> 00:39:38.308
l checked myself in
when l was 22.


00:39:40.747 --> 00:39:43.682
l was in grad school.
l was under a lot of stress.


00:39:43.716 --> 00:39:46.685
l was there for three days.
That's it.


00:39:46.719 --> 00:39:48.983
l don't see how
that's relevant.


00:39:49.022 --> 00:39:52.458
What are you doing
on antidepressants?


00:39:52.492 --> 00:39:54.926
Oh, you think
l'm making this up.


00:39:56.095 --> 00:39:58.655
You think that,


00:39:58.698 --> 00:40:01.667
what, my imaginary
boyfriend went missing?


00:40:01.701 --> 00:40:03.635
You're an only child.


00:40:03.670 --> 00:40:05.365
Your father left
when you were young.


00:40:05.405 --> 00:40:08.863
Your mother died
earlier this year


00:40:08.908 --> 00:40:10.671
in a hospital.


00:40:10.710 --> 00:40:14.111
Yes, February.


00:40:14.147 --> 00:40:17.207
She went in
for a routine check-up


00:40:17.250 --> 00:40:19.013
and never checked out.


00:40:19.052 --> 00:40:21.520
She had a blood infection.


00:40:21.554 --> 00:40:23.886
So it's not surprising
that your subconscious


00:40:23.923 --> 00:40:26.687
would choose a hospital
to fabricate--


00:40:26.726 --> 00:40:30.162
lt's not my subconscious
anything.


00:40:30.196 --> 00:40:32.027
Oh my Lord!


00:40:32.065 --> 00:40:34.590
This is real.


00:40:37.003 --> 00:40:39.528
He was there for me.


00:40:39.572 --> 00:40:42.507
You know, l remember
her funeral.


00:40:42.542 --> 00:40:45.272
- He was at it.
- Kevin?


00:40:45.311 --> 00:40:47.279
Yes, Kevin.


00:40:47.313 --> 00:40:50.908
l know it's hard to lose somebody
you care deeply about, Mary.


00:40:50.950 --> 00:40:53.612
lt's very understandable
how someone in your situation


00:40:53.653 --> 00:40:55.450
could suffer
a psychological break.


00:40:55.488 --> 00:40:57.353
You work long hours.


00:40:57.390 --> 00:40:59.449
You've lost your emotional
support system. You're alone.


00:40:59.492 --> 00:41:01.460
lt's only natural for the brain
to reach for something,


00:41:01.494 --> 00:41:03.121
anything, to grab onto.


00:41:03.162 --> 00:41:05.357
He drove us here.


00:41:05.398 --> 00:41:06.922
He did.


00:41:06.966 --> 00:41:10.595
And l remember the ride
like the back of my hand.


00:41:10.636 --> 00:41:12.934
He-- he-- he was--


00:41:12.972 --> 00:41:15.099
He was chewing on the lid
of his coffee cup.


00:41:15.141 --> 00:41:18.907
- lt's this little nervous habit that he has.
- Sorry.


00:41:18.945 --> 00:41:20.412
l know that it all
must seem real.


00:41:20.446 --> 00:41:22.778
lt seems real
because it is real!


00:41:24.050 --> 00:41:27.577
l remember walking through
the parking structure.


00:41:27.620 --> 00:41:30.714
Memory is a very vivid
and powerful sensation, Mary.


00:41:30.757 --> 00:41:32.224
lt is real!


00:41:32.258 --> 00:41:34.590
This whole situation
is real.


00:41:34.627 --> 00:41:37.061
And he's here.
He was here,


00:41:37.096 --> 00:41:40.361
He's somewhere
right now in this hospital


00:41:40.399 --> 00:41:42.594
and we're wasting time!


00:41:44.170 --> 00:41:47.537
The nurse advised me
to get coffee,


00:41:47.573 --> 00:41:49.734
said the surgery
would be an hour.


00:41:49.776 --> 00:41:53.212
lt was 25 minutes,
and he's gone.


00:41:54.547 --> 00:41:56.014
lt was real.


00:41:56.048 --> 00:41:58.312
lt's all right, Mary.


00:41:58.351 --> 00:42:00.319
Can l just have
a moment alone?


00:42:00.353 --> 00:42:02.321
Take all the time
you need, dear.


00:42:02.355 --> 00:42:04.550
l'll be in my office
next door.


00:42:04.590 --> 00:42:06.683
Okay.


00:42:57.610 --> 00:42:59.703
Mary, l--


00:43:04.116 --> 00:43:06.414
Security.


00:43:38.517 --> 00:43:40.508
Want some company?


00:43:48.494 --> 00:43:51.861
Do you know l was just here
for a checkup today?


00:43:53.599 --> 00:43:55.760
Doctor told me l need
to take it easy.


00:43:58.104 --> 00:43:59.799
Then you call.


00:43:59.839 --> 00:44:03.502
l gotta tell you, this job can really
take its toll on you--


00:44:04.610 --> 00:44:06.601
your health,
your marriage.


00:44:06.646 --> 00:44:08.113
You're married?


00:44:08.147 --> 00:44:11.378
Was.


00:44:11.417 --> 00:44:14.784
Marriage, it can be
a funny thing, you know?


00:44:14.820 --> 00:44:18.278
You commit yourself,
you hand your heart over to someone,


00:44:18.324 --> 00:44:22.226
but it always seems like
it's the little things


00:44:22.261 --> 00:44:24.786
that keep
chipping away at it--


00:44:24.830 --> 00:44:27.355
Little disagreements.


00:44:27.400 --> 00:44:29.391
She--


00:44:29.435 --> 00:44:31.869
she hated the fact
that l was a cop.


00:44:31.904 --> 00:44:34.202
And you know what?


00:44:34.240 --> 00:44:37.141
Maybe--
maybe she was right.


00:44:37.176 --> 00:44:38.666
l don't know.


00:44:41.213 --> 00:44:44.671
l was working a gang shooting
over in Glassell Park,


00:44:44.717 --> 00:44:47.345
and my partner and l,


00:44:47.386 --> 00:44:49.854
we traced the shooter back
to his girlfriend's house.


00:44:49.889 --> 00:44:53.381
He'd been shacking up there
for a couple of weeks.


00:44:54.460 --> 00:44:56.428
And we had the kid cornered,
so we went in.


00:44:56.462 --> 00:44:59.124
He was unarmed,
gave himself right up.


00:45:03.669 --> 00:45:07.435
What we didn't know that his girlfriend
was in the house.


00:45:14.480 --> 00:45:17.506
The last thing l remember
before l blacked out...


00:45:20.453 --> 00:45:22.478
was watching my partner...


00:45:25.057 --> 00:45:27.855
his dark lifeless eyes


00:45:27.893 --> 00:45:29.986
as he fell to the floor.


00:45:38.804 --> 00:45:40.328
Now look at me.


00:45:40.373 --> 00:45:42.705
l've got a desk job
and high blood pressure


00:45:42.742 --> 00:45:46.473
and a doctor telling me
how to live my life.


00:45:46.512 --> 00:45:48.980
What l'm--


00:45:49.015 --> 00:45:51.006
what l'm trying
to say here is that...


00:45:54.020 --> 00:45:57.285
l understand what
you're going through.


00:46:02.695 --> 00:46:06.654
Can you please tell
Dr. Bensley


00:46:06.699 --> 00:46:08.690
that...


00:46:10.403 --> 00:46:14.066
he can just do whatever needs to do,
all right?


00:46:41.300 --> 00:46:43.291
Mary's behavior
is definitely indicative


00:46:43.335 --> 00:46:46.327
of someone in the midst
of an emotional breakdown.


00:46:46.372 --> 00:46:49.068
And yet l never met anyone
with such conviction


00:46:49.108 --> 00:46:51.406
in her delusion.


00:46:51.444 --> 00:46:54.277
She absolutely believes that everything
that's happening is real.


00:46:55.748 --> 00:46:58.842
She's emotionally lost.


00:46:58.884 --> 00:47:00.875
( click )


00:47:02.888 --> 00:47:06.619
- ( dials phone )
- ( rings )


00:47:06.659 --> 00:47:08.217
Yeah, this Bensley.


00:47:08.260 --> 00:47:11.855
Listen, l wanna put Mary Walsh
under 72-hour observation.


00:47:13.032 --> 00:47:16.263
Mm-hmm.
Possible mental illness.


00:47:16.302 --> 00:47:18.827
( dial tone hums )


00:47:44.563 --> 00:47:48.260
Mr. Holloway,
this is J.J.


00:47:48.300 --> 00:47:49.597
l have her
in the hallway.


00:47:49.635 --> 00:47:51.830
Switching to camera 2.


00:47:51.871 --> 00:47:54.533
l'm following her
along the hallway.


00:47:55.908 --> 00:47:58.138
- J.J.: l have her.
- Do not lose her.


00:47:58.177 --> 00:48:01.578
Sir, it looks like she's heading towards
sublevel ''B''-- boiler room and laundry.


00:48:01.614 --> 00:48:03.775
We only have limited
coverage down there.


00:48:03.816 --> 00:48:06.546
l'm en route right now.


00:48:57.236 --> 00:48:58.794
Dr. Bensley, what are
we dealing with here?


00:48:58.837 --> 00:49:00.361
ls she dangerous?


00:49:00.406 --> 00:49:02.033
lt's impossible to say.


00:49:02.074 --> 00:49:04.941
Acute perception
of persecution, paranoia.


00:49:04.977 --> 00:49:07.844
You just never know
how someone like this will act


00:49:07.880 --> 00:49:10.075
when pushed too far.


00:49:15.654 --> 00:49:19.590
No, no.
No cameras, none.


00:49:19.625 --> 00:49:22.389
No parking lot.
No exits.


00:49:22.428 --> 00:49:24.293
No. l can't find
her anywhere.


00:49:24.330 --> 00:49:26.491
We only got a couple of cameras
operational in that area,


00:49:26.532 --> 00:49:28.727
so it's not gonna be easy.
l'm gonna keep on scanning.


00:49:28.767 --> 00:49:30.735
Wait, l think
l've got something.


00:49:30.769 --> 00:49:33.431
Boom! Camera 4 in the boiler room.
She's wearing blue scrubs.


00:49:33.472 --> 00:49:35.440
lt looks like she's heading
towards the morgue.


00:49:35.474 --> 00:49:37.908
She's running. She's on the move.
l'm gonna lose her.


00:50:02.134 --> 00:50:04.659
You had a chance to talk with her.
ls she currently on meds?


00:50:04.703 --> 00:50:06.637
Yeah, quite
a potent dosage.


00:50:06.672 --> 00:50:09.869
Okay, so this could be some sort
of psychotic reaction.


00:50:09.908 --> 00:50:12.103
lt could indeed.


00:50:12.144 --> 00:50:14.612
( panting )


00:50:14.647 --> 00:50:18.276
( cell phone rings )


00:50:19.952 --> 00:50:21.920
Hello.


00:50:21.954 --> 00:50:25.822
Kevin:
Hello, it's me.


00:50:25.858 --> 00:50:28.224
My God, Kevin.


00:50:28.260 --> 00:50:30.285
Where are you?


00:50:30.329 --> 00:50:32.854
l don't know.
Somewhere in the hospital.


00:50:34.433 --> 00:50:36.333
What's happening?


00:50:36.368 --> 00:50:38.495
Listen to me, okay?


00:50:38.537 --> 00:50:41.005
Don't trust anyone.


00:50:41.040 --> 00:50:43.099
l don't know how many people
are involved in this.


00:50:43.142 --> 00:50:44.803
lt's very important,
okay?


00:50:44.843 --> 00:50:47.676
- What do they want?
- l don't know.


00:50:47.713 --> 00:50:51.114
J.J.: She has to be close by.
She couldn't have gone too far.


00:50:51.150 --> 00:50:54.313
Check all the rooms
on that wing.


00:50:54.353 --> 00:50:56.787
Look around you. Where are you?
Where are you right now?


00:50:56.822 --> 00:50:59.017
l'm in a bathroom
somewhere.


00:50:59.058 --> 00:51:00.685
Are you okay?
Are you safe?


00:51:00.726 --> 00:51:02.591
Where are you?


00:51:02.628 --> 00:51:04.186
l don't-- hold on.


00:51:07.900 --> 00:51:10.596
( gasps )


00:51:10.636 --> 00:51:12.160
Um...


00:51:12.204 --> 00:51:14.297
l'm in the morgue.


00:51:14.340 --> 00:51:16.808
- Can you get down here?
- No, no! Leave me alone!


00:51:16.842 --> 00:51:19.504
Kevin.


00:51:19.545 --> 00:51:22.981
Kevin. Kevin!


00:51:23.015 --> 00:51:25.210
Kevin.


00:51:25.250 --> 00:51:27.775
( gasps )


00:51:35.527 --> 00:51:37.518
Miss Walsh.


00:51:39.031 --> 00:51:41.761
Miss Walsh, you in here?


00:52:30.682 --> 00:52:33.583
J.J.: l got her. She's heading
towards the parking garage.


00:52:40.993 --> 00:52:43.826
- ( screams )
- ( brakes screech )


00:52:48.267 --> 00:52:50.326
Oh my God! Oh my God!
Are you all right?


00:52:50.369 --> 00:52:52.769
Are you all right?


00:52:52.805 --> 00:52:55.273
This is a first date.


00:52:55.307 --> 00:52:57.832
- We don't kiss on the first date.
- Third. Fifth date.


00:53:03.816 --> 00:53:06.444
( indistinct )


00:53:48.861 --> 00:53:50.920
Gonna wait?
This could take awhile.


00:53:55.834 --> 00:53:57.859
l think l've done
all l can do.


00:53:57.903 --> 00:54:01.066
Sorry she sent you
on such a wild goose chase.


00:54:01.106 --> 00:54:04.735
Yeah, it happens.


00:54:06.645 --> 00:54:09.170
- Good afternoon, Doc.
- Detective.


00:54:42.080 --> 00:54:44.071
Cooper: Hi, Mary.


00:54:45.784 --> 00:54:48.014
- Hello.
- Shh.


00:54:49.354 --> 00:54:52.323
l heard what happened.
These are for you.


00:54:54.660 --> 00:54:57.458
Hey, it's gonna be okay.


00:54:57.496 --> 00:55:00.294
The doctor thought you needed
some more time to recuperate.


00:55:00.332 --> 00:55:03.062
The cop-- l think
he might have left.


00:55:03.101 --> 00:55:05.194
Thank you.


00:55:09.775 --> 00:55:11.743
They think l'm crazy.


00:55:11.777 --> 00:55:13.472
l'm not.


00:55:13.512 --> 00:55:15.104
l'm not crazy.


00:55:15.147 --> 00:55:18.639
No, you're not crazy.
That's why l came down here.


00:55:18.684 --> 00:55:20.879
l want to discuss the situation
about Kevin


00:55:20.919 --> 00:55:22.887
and how you could
see him again.


00:55:22.921 --> 00:55:24.548
You do wanna see
him again, right?


00:55:24.590 --> 00:55:26.057
Do you know
where he is?


00:55:26.091 --> 00:55:28.616
Now don't get yourself
worked up, young lady.


00:55:30.963 --> 00:55:33.864
You did make quite a spectacle
of yourself, Miss Walsh.


00:55:33.899 --> 00:55:36.629
The emotional outburst,
the panicking.


00:55:36.668 --> 00:55:39.762
We expected that,
but the accident.


00:55:39.805 --> 00:55:43.002
Oh, my my, Mary, l mean,
you've got to be more careful.


00:55:46.511 --> 00:55:50.470
''Mary Catherine Walsh, unmarried,
regional operations manager


00:55:50.515 --> 00:55:52.608
for the Empyrean
lnternational Bank.''


00:55:52.651 --> 00:55:56.018
You rent a condo in Reseda.
Your mother died four months ago,


00:55:56.054 --> 00:55:59.148
but the bank got your house
in the reverse mortgage.


00:55:59.191 --> 00:56:01.819
That's true.


00:56:01.860 --> 00:56:05.421
- How do you know this?
- l did my research.


00:56:05.464 --> 00:56:07.022
But your bank,
on the other hand,


00:56:07.065 --> 00:56:09.363
recently received
from the federal government


00:56:09.401 --> 00:56:11.335
a $2 billion bailout.


00:56:11.370 --> 00:56:13.895
Now l've seen
the bonus structure,


00:56:13.939 --> 00:56:15.839
rewarding
their executives


00:56:15.874 --> 00:56:19.037
while letting their customers
go bankrupt, huh?


00:56:19.077 --> 00:56:23.070
And you have access
to unlimited funds.


00:56:28.020 --> 00:56:31.615
Don't you hurt him.
Don't you hurt him!


00:56:35.060 --> 00:56:37.051
So...


00:56:38.530 --> 00:56:41.124
- How much?
- $10 million.


00:56:41.166 --> 00:56:44.135
l've taken the liberty
to get Kevin's computer.


00:56:44.169 --> 00:56:47.730
lnside here you'll find the account
and wire routing numbers


00:56:47.773 --> 00:56:49.673
of a bank account
in the Cayman lslands.


00:56:49.708 --> 00:56:51.835
Once l receive confirmation
of funds received,


00:56:51.877 --> 00:56:54.402
l'll let your boyfriend go.


00:56:59.685 --> 00:57:01.710
Shit.


00:57:05.724 --> 00:57:07.351
l have no Wi-Fi signal.


00:57:07.392 --> 00:57:09.053
l checked it myself.
lt's fine.


00:57:09.094 --> 00:57:11.028
Yeah, l don't have a wireless signal
in this room.


00:57:11.063 --> 00:57:12.928
l need a hard line.


00:57:12.964 --> 00:57:16.161
l need to move
to a different location.


00:57:16.201 --> 00:57:18.465
Yeah, it's me.


00:57:18.503 --> 00:57:20.198
Yeah, cut off
Peterson's finger.


00:57:20.238 --> 00:57:23.173
No, wait! Wait!
Tell him no.


00:57:23.208 --> 00:57:25.574
Look at this right here.


00:57:25.610 --> 00:57:28.477
This is our signal.
There is none.


00:57:28.513 --> 00:57:31.641
l've tried every
single network,


00:57:31.683 --> 00:57:34.174
- and there's nothing.
- Hold that for one second.


00:57:34.219 --> 00:57:36.687
l need you to move me
to a place


00:57:36.722 --> 00:57:39.122
where l can plug in
a different computer.


00:57:39.157 --> 00:57:40.954
l can get it done
in no time, okay?


00:57:40.992 --> 00:57:44.951
Yeah, all right.


00:57:44.996 --> 00:57:47.294
l've got 26 minutes till the cutoff,
which is exactly how much time


00:57:47.332 --> 00:57:50.460
you've got to find a computer
to get me my money.


00:57:50.502 --> 00:57:52.595
You're being watched.
We know everything you do.


00:57:52.637 --> 00:57:55.299
lf you fail, Kevin dies.


00:57:55.340 --> 00:57:57.308
lf you tell anyone,
Kevin dies.


00:57:57.342 --> 00:58:00.175
lf you leave the hospital,
Kevin dies.


00:58:01.446 --> 00:58:02.879
Got it.


00:58:02.914 --> 00:58:05.439
Here's your clothing.
l found it downstairs.


00:58:05.484 --> 00:58:08.976
Meet me on sublevel ''B''
when you're done.


00:58:10.822 --> 00:58:12.585
Wonderful.


00:58:57.068 --> 00:58:59.059
Miss Walsh?


00:59:14.920 --> 00:59:17.855
( typing )


00:59:32.103 --> 00:59:35.334
Mr. Holloway, that crazy
Mary Walsh lady is back


00:59:35.373 --> 00:59:37.341
wandering the halls.


00:59:37.375 --> 00:59:39.343
She's looking for a patient
that does not appear to be in our system.


00:59:39.377 --> 00:59:41.345
She needs be escorted
out immediately.


00:59:41.379 --> 00:59:43.370
- l'll alert Miss Markham.
- Thank you.


01:00:17.616 --> 01:00:20.881
We have footage of Miss Walsh
in the trauma recovery room.


01:00:20.919 --> 01:00:22.887
J.J., punch up everything on level 3,
would you, please?


01:00:22.921 --> 01:00:24.582
- Thank you.
- You got it.


01:00:27.425 --> 01:00:30.258
- Holloway: There you go.
- l wanted somebody on that door.


01:00:30.295 --> 01:00:32.263
Unfortunately,
the nurse stepped away.


01:00:32.297 --> 01:00:34.288
You don't really think
she's dangerous, do you?


01:00:34.332 --> 01:00:36.300
l'm not taking
any chances.


01:00:36.334 --> 01:00:39.167
Besides, with her injuries,
her well-being is my responsibility.


01:00:39.204 --> 01:00:41.229
Trust me. She's still here,
and we will find her.


01:00:41.273 --> 01:00:43.798
l have my people turning
this place upside down.


01:00:43.842 --> 01:00:45.434
Well, let me know the minute
you hear anything.


01:00:45.477 --> 01:00:47.035
l'm going back upstairs.


01:00:47.078 --> 01:00:49.478
You got it, Miss Markham.
Thank you.


01:01:22.714 --> 01:01:24.739
( typing )


01:01:24.783 --> 01:01:26.774
( elevator bell dings )


01:01:58.249 --> 01:02:00.012
$10 million.


01:02:04.522 --> 01:02:06.717
$10 million.


01:02:44.129 --> 01:02:45.756
Please work.


01:03:50.128 --> 01:03:52.562
( exhales )


01:04:05.810 --> 01:04:08.438
Hello.


01:04:08.480 --> 01:04:10.573
- ( Kevin grunting )
- Mary: Kevin.


01:04:10.615 --> 01:04:14.346
- Mary, Mary.
- Oh, Kevin.


01:04:16.354 --> 01:04:18.117
Are you hurt?


01:04:18.156 --> 01:04:19.646
He's fine.


01:04:19.691 --> 01:04:21.591
Let him go.


01:04:21.626 --> 01:04:25.027
- The receipt.
- l need to email a confirmation code


01:04:25.063 --> 01:04:26.860
to complete
the wire transfer.


01:04:26.898 --> 01:04:30.800
So l would suggest
that you let him go now.


01:04:51.422 --> 01:04:53.447
Move it!


01:04:55.593 --> 01:04:58.994
Honey.


01:04:59.030 --> 01:05:00.895
l thought l lost
you forever.


01:05:00.932 --> 01:05:02.559
The code, come on!


01:05:02.600 --> 01:05:05.228
Done.


01:05:05.270 --> 01:05:07.033
Come on, let's go
up those stairs.


01:05:07.071 --> 01:05:10.199
We could get away.
Just go right up those stairs.


01:05:17.615 --> 01:05:19.708
Well, l'm glad
you made it safely.


01:05:19.751 --> 01:05:21.218
l understand you're from Missouri.
ls that correct?


01:05:21.252 --> 01:05:22.378
Yeah, Kansas City.


01:05:22.420 --> 01:05:25.412
- ls that near St. Louis?
- Other side of the state.


01:05:25.456 --> 01:05:27.117
- Excuse me one second.
- ( cell phone rings )


01:05:27.158 --> 01:05:28.887
Royal Cayman Bank & Trust.
This is Barry.


01:05:28.927 --> 01:05:32.419
Yeah, Conyers.
Yeah, it's me.


01:05:32.463 --> 01:05:33.987
Did it go through?


01:05:34.032 --> 01:05:37.263
Yes, sir. As a matter of fact,
it's pending right now.


01:05:37.302 --> 01:05:39.827
We're on, guys.


01:05:39.871 --> 01:05:41.429
Thank you, Miss Walsh.


01:05:45.877 --> 01:05:47.504
Great work, baby.


01:05:47.545 --> 01:05:51.106
l mean, fantastic.


01:05:54.385 --> 01:05:56.615
Kevin: lt's a good thing too.
Just in time,


01:05:56.654 --> 01:05:59.623
'cause this brace is really starting
to make my leg really stiff.


01:06:02.093 --> 01:06:04.061
Kevin,
what are you doing?


01:06:04.095 --> 01:06:07.121
Cooper: Haven't you been paying any
attention? There is no Kevin Peterson.


01:06:08.299 --> 01:06:10.062
Kevin.


01:06:12.270 --> 01:06:13.965
Oh my God.
Where are you?


01:06:14.005 --> 01:06:17.805
l don't know.
l'm in the hospital somewhere.


01:06:17.842 --> 01:06:19.810
Can you get down here?


01:06:19.844 --> 01:06:22.438
- No, no, leave me alone!
- Kevin.


01:06:23.948 --> 01:06:27.611
There is no...


01:06:27.652 --> 01:06:30.621
Kevin Peterson.


01:06:32.023 --> 01:06:34.924
Kevin, Kevin!


01:06:36.127 --> 01:06:38.095
( groans )


01:06:38.129 --> 01:06:39.153
Kevin.


01:06:39.197 --> 01:06:41.665
( camera shutter clicks )


01:06:43.134 --> 01:06:46.570
Don't you hurt him.
Don't you hurt him.


01:06:46.604 --> 01:06:48.071
Oh, my.


01:06:48.106 --> 01:06:51.234
So how much?


01:06:57.548 --> 01:06:59.982
- ( laughing )
- Franklin: What about the nurse,


01:07:00.018 --> 01:07:02.077
this Amanda?


01:07:02.120 --> 01:07:04.486
- So you must be Kevin Peterson.
- Yeah.


01:07:04.522 --> 01:07:06.490
- l'm Amanda.
- Markham: We don't have anyone


01:07:06.524 --> 01:07:09.015
- by that name.
- See you in an hour.


01:07:10.061 --> 01:07:12.188
- Mary: Lovely nurse came in to prep him.
- What was the nurse's name?


01:07:12.230 --> 01:07:14.357
Mary: Uh, no...
( snaps fingers ) Amanda.


01:07:14.399 --> 01:07:18.199
- My boyfriend is Kevin Peterson...
- Come here, come here.


01:07:18.236 --> 01:07:20.101
...and we can't find him.


01:07:20.138 --> 01:07:23.869
My wife,
she has breast cancer.


01:07:23.908 --> 01:07:26.843
Well, she's up in chemo.


01:07:26.878 --> 01:07:29.176
That's him
right there.


01:07:29.213 --> 01:07:32.011
Color accuracy is difficult to determine
with closed-circuit cameras.


01:07:32.050 --> 01:07:36.350
You know, Detective Franklin,
we have people here she can talk to.


01:07:36.387 --> 01:07:39.550
l'm sure Miss Markham could
arrange something, if need be.


01:07:39.590 --> 01:07:41.820
Mary:
Everything is a lie?


01:07:41.859 --> 01:07:44.157
Everything
is a lie?


01:07:44.195 --> 01:07:46.595
Every-- every--
everything--


01:07:46.631 --> 01:07:50.567
- everything is a lie.
- Don't take it personally, Mare.


01:07:50.601 --> 01:07:53.331
- Mare bear.
- Don't touch me.


01:07:53.371 --> 01:07:55.532
The man you fell
in love with...


01:07:57.608 --> 01:07:59.371
he's not real.


01:07:59.410 --> 01:08:02.004
l'm a real idiot.


01:08:12.924 --> 01:08:15.518
( sighs )


01:08:15.560 --> 01:08:18.893
Didn't he tell you about his time in prison?
That's where l met the guy.


01:08:18.930 --> 01:08:21.364
Believe me, if l was any younger,
l would have done this myself.


01:08:21.399 --> 01:08:24.493
No no no, Coop.
You couldn't handle her.


01:08:24.535 --> 01:08:27.060
She's a real tiger cat
between the sheets.


01:08:27.105 --> 01:08:29.699
Oh, l don't know, Coop.


01:08:29.741 --> 01:08:33.199
l think you could
have handled her.


01:08:34.812 --> 01:08:36.279
Holloway: All we had
to do was sit back


01:08:36.314 --> 01:08:39.044
and watch you lose it.
lt was simple.


01:08:39.083 --> 01:08:42.450
Mare bear,
for old times' sake.


01:08:42.487 --> 01:08:45.081
- Come on in.
- Don't you dare touch me.


01:08:45.123 --> 01:08:47.683
- Don't touch me.
- Allow me.


01:08:47.725 --> 01:08:49.920
Boys, l think
it's time to go.


01:08:49.961 --> 01:08:52.862
All right, Holloway,
you know the drill.


01:08:52.897 --> 01:08:54.364
Amanda.


01:08:54.399 --> 01:08:56.731
l'll send you a postcard.


01:09:02.039 --> 01:09:04.269
( softly )
l'm sorry.


01:09:15.153 --> 01:09:18.418
Victoria Markham's
office, please.


01:09:20.024 --> 01:09:23.050
lt's Detective Franklin.
Tell her it's urgent.


01:09:23.094 --> 01:09:25.961
What do you mean she disappeared?
Where'd she go?


01:09:27.632 --> 01:09:30.658
Look, l think she's telling us the truth
about her boyfriend.


01:09:30.701 --> 01:09:32.669
She's messed up in something.
l don't know what it is.


01:09:32.703 --> 01:09:35.467
l think she's in some kind of trouble.
Just find her.


01:09:35.506 --> 01:09:38.100
Just find her!
l'm on my way there right now.


01:09:53.524 --> 01:09:56.015
Whoo!


01:09:56.060 --> 01:09:58.654
$10 million feels good,
doesn't it, babe?


01:09:58.696 --> 01:10:00.288
Baby, gimme a kiss.


01:10:16.380 --> 01:10:19.645
You know,
l almost feel bad.


01:10:19.684 --> 01:10:22.209
Amanda:
Oh, yeah, why is that?


01:10:22.253 --> 01:10:26.246
Almost, but l can think of
10 million reasons why not.


01:10:27.425 --> 01:10:30.724
( laughing )
Come on! Up!


01:10:30.761 --> 01:10:32.695
Get up those stairs.
Come on!


01:10:32.730 --> 01:10:36.427
- Don't fight me!
- ( shrieks )


01:10:36.467 --> 01:10:39.834
Yeah, you're a fighter,
ain't you?


01:10:43.407 --> 01:10:47.241
l believe Stevie once said
you were an animal in bed.


01:10:47.278 --> 01:10:50.247
- ( gasping )
- Easy easy.


01:10:50.281 --> 01:10:52.476
Shh!


01:10:52.517 --> 01:10:55.179
Yeah.
( laughing )


01:10:55.219 --> 01:10:57.483
Yeah.


01:10:57.522 --> 01:10:59.183
Damn, you're fine.


01:10:59.223 --> 01:11:02.249
l wanna show you something.


01:11:02.293 --> 01:11:04.318
- All right.
- Yeah.


01:11:04.362 --> 01:11:06.762
Maybe l shouldn't let
you go just yet.


01:11:09.534 --> 01:11:11.229
What are you reaching
for down there?


01:11:11.269 --> 01:11:13.601
- lt's my phone.
- What about your phone?


01:11:13.638 --> 01:11:16.664
The transfer.


01:11:16.707 --> 01:11:19.437
You know they were talking
about the transfer?


01:11:19.477 --> 01:11:21.604
Yeah, what about it?


01:11:21.646 --> 01:11:23.273
lt's still pending.


01:11:23.314 --> 01:11:26.715
Really? You pulling another one
of your tiger moves?


01:11:26.751 --> 01:11:29.276
- ls that it?
- l could take that money


01:11:29.320 --> 01:11:31.447
and l could transfer it
right into your account


01:11:31.489 --> 01:11:33.457
with just the click
of a button.


01:11:33.491 --> 01:11:35.686
What do you mean
l could have the money?


01:11:35.726 --> 01:11:37.660
l'll prove it to you.
l'll do it right here. Look.


01:11:37.695 --> 01:11:40.459
Slowly, do it slowly.


01:11:40.498 --> 01:11:44.127
Let me see. Oh!


01:11:44.168 --> 01:11:46.898
( grunts )


01:11:46.938 --> 01:11:50.066
( shouts )


01:12:06.724 --> 01:12:10.490
Mary,
where's my little lamb?


01:12:11.829 --> 01:12:15.094
Mary!
Where you at?


01:12:27.011 --> 01:12:29.002
Holloway:
Mary!


01:12:30.214 --> 01:12:33.308
Mary.


01:12:36.053 --> 01:12:38.487
We got 23 exits.


01:12:38.522 --> 01:12:41.286
We checked 22.


01:12:44.562 --> 01:12:47.258
( panting )


01:12:47.298 --> 01:12:49.232
( moans )


01:12:50.635 --> 01:12:53.126
Really? You think
l did a good job?


01:12:53.204 --> 01:12:55.297
Yes, you in the naughty
nurse's outfit


01:12:55.339 --> 01:12:58.137
was
really something.


01:12:58.175 --> 01:13:00.700
Thanks, baby.
l was so nervous.


01:13:00.745 --> 01:13:03.509
Hey, look,
don't get too excited.


01:13:03.547 --> 01:13:06.880
- Give Holloway a call.
- All right.


01:13:06.917 --> 01:13:09.909
( cell phone ringing )


01:13:24.035 --> 01:13:27.368
- ( beep )
- Kevin: Hello, Holloway.


01:13:27.405 --> 01:13:31.000
( Mary panting )


01:13:31.042 --> 01:13:34.136
Sounds like you're
out of breath.


01:13:34.178 --> 01:13:36.510
Mare bear...


01:13:36.547 --> 01:13:38.208
is that you?


01:13:40.284 --> 01:13:43.617
l can hear you breathing.


01:13:43.654 --> 01:13:45.144
And l know your breath.


01:13:45.189 --> 01:13:47.987
Where's Holloway?


01:13:48.025 --> 01:13:51.825
You didn't kill
Holloway, did you?


01:13:51.862 --> 01:13:55.389
l didn't know
you had it in you.


01:13:55.433 --> 01:13:57.492
Mary.


01:13:57.535 --> 01:13:59.196
Mary, listen to me.


01:13:59.236 --> 01:14:01.602
l'm coming for you, Mary.
l'm coming down there.


01:14:01.639 --> 01:14:04.130
You just stay put, sweets.
We can sort this all out.


01:14:04.175 --> 01:14:06.336
l'm coming for you.
Damn it!


01:14:06.377 --> 01:14:08.868
Holloway screwed up.
She's not dead.


01:14:08.913 --> 01:14:12.041
Just relax. l'll get the money, okay?
We'll get the money!


01:14:12.083 --> 01:14:14.051
l thought you said
you knew this chick, Steve.


01:14:14.085 --> 01:14:17.020
- l do. l told you, she's smart.
- ( cell phone rings )


01:14:17.054 --> 01:14:20.512
- Hello.
- Barry: l'm afraid there's been a problem.


01:14:20.558 --> 01:14:22.048
The wire's
been reversed.


01:14:22.093 --> 01:14:23.458
Cooper:
What are you talking about?


01:14:23.494 --> 01:14:25.462
The bank recalled
the money.


01:14:25.496 --> 01:14:27.828
Can't do that.


01:14:27.865 --> 01:14:30.356
- lt's not my call, sir.
- That's not good enough.


01:14:30.401 --> 01:14:32.665
Sir, there's nothing more
that l can do, okay?


01:14:32.703 --> 01:14:35.638
lt's not on my end.
l did what you told me to do.


01:14:35.673 --> 01:14:38.403
- l did what you asked me to do.
- l'll get them to rescind it.


01:14:38.442 --> 01:14:40.569
Sir, do whatever
you have to do, sir.


01:14:40.611 --> 01:14:43.603
l'm sorry.


01:14:45.249 --> 01:14:48.116
We gotta go back.
Get us back to the hospital.


01:14:48.152 --> 01:14:50.586
l'll take care
of it myself.


01:14:50.621 --> 01:14:53.613
l'll put a bullet
in her head right now.


01:14:53.657 --> 01:14:55.750
Turn around here.


01:14:57.628 --> 01:14:59.596
Son of a bitch!


01:15:29.527 --> 01:15:31.154
There she is!


01:15:31.195 --> 01:15:34.358
( tires screeching )


01:15:42.406 --> 01:15:45.000
- ( crash )
- ( car alarm blaring )


01:16:04.395 --> 01:16:06.693
End of the road, baby.


01:16:06.730 --> 01:16:09.722
All right, you take the wheel.
Meet us topside.


01:16:21.512 --> 01:16:24.242
Woman:
All units, three armed suspects


01:16:24.281 --> 01:16:26.841
spotted in hospital parking garage
driving silver sedan.


01:16:26.884 --> 01:16:29.580
All units respond.


01:16:40.898 --> 01:16:44.265
Shh shh shh.
Wait wait.


01:16:55.045 --> 01:16:56.945
( horn honks )


01:16:56.981 --> 01:16:59.779
( crash )


01:17:08.893 --> 01:17:10.690
- Where'd they go?
- l don't know.


01:17:10.728 --> 01:17:12.958
- Where'd they go?
- They went that way.


01:17:12.997 --> 01:17:15.727
- Chill out!
- You stay right here.


01:17:15.766 --> 01:17:16.824
You hear me?
Right here!


01:17:21.071 --> 01:17:23.699
l need backup
at County Hospital now.


01:17:23.741 --> 01:17:26.608
Mary honey,
l'm not gonna hurt you.


01:17:34.952 --> 01:17:36.943
( silent )


01:17:56.440 --> 01:17:59.034
Mare bear.


01:18:04.014 --> 01:18:07.074
No! No, don't hit her.
We need her information.


01:18:07.117 --> 01:18:09.847
Honey, Mary.
He's sorry.


01:18:16.293 --> 01:18:18.284
Mare.


01:18:55.599 --> 01:18:57.032
Mary: Please stop!


01:18:57.067 --> 01:19:00.298
Cooper, put the gun down.


01:19:00.337 --> 01:19:02.532
You're a smart girl,
Walsh.


01:19:02.573 --> 01:19:05.406
There's no good way out of this.
Don't be stupid.


01:19:05.442 --> 01:19:08.411
l'm gonna put my gun down.


01:19:08.445 --> 01:19:10.242
l'm gonna do it
right here.


01:19:10.280 --> 01:19:13.716
l'll go my way.
You go yours, okay?


01:19:15.285 --> 01:19:17.753
Drop your weapon,
Cooper.


01:19:22.192 --> 01:19:24.422
( gasps )


01:19:26.096 --> 01:19:29.429
Coop...


01:19:29.466 --> 01:19:31.457
you okay?


01:19:51.688 --> 01:19:54.213
Kevin:
Whoa whoa whoa!


01:19:54.258 --> 01:19:56.226
Where'd you get a gun,
honey?


01:19:56.260 --> 01:19:58.285
Put it away.
Stay where you are.


01:19:58.328 --> 01:20:02.196
Whoa whoa whoa.
Baby, l'll put this away.


01:20:02.232 --> 01:20:04.564
Take it easy.


01:20:04.601 --> 01:20:08.037
This is a whole
different side of you


01:20:08.072 --> 01:20:09.903
l've never seen.


01:20:09.940 --> 01:20:13.432
And how do you feel
about that side?


01:20:13.477 --> 01:20:15.911
l like it.


01:20:15.946 --> 01:20:17.880
l like it a lot.


01:20:17.915 --> 01:20:20.383
Me too.


01:20:20.417 --> 01:20:23.386
Baby, this whole thing
has gotten completely


01:20:23.420 --> 01:20:25.217
out of hand.


01:20:25.255 --> 01:20:26.950
You were never
supposed to get hurt.


01:20:26.990 --> 01:20:28.981
Okay?


01:20:29.026 --> 01:20:31.290
Look,
we can work this out.


01:20:31.328 --> 01:20:34.491
Okay, listen,


01:20:34.531 --> 01:20:37.898
forget these guys, okay?


01:20:37.935 --> 01:20:41.166
Why don't you and l
just take the money?


01:20:41.205 --> 01:20:42.934
You can resend it.


01:20:42.973 --> 01:20:45.965
We'll take it. We can be anybody
we wanna be.


01:20:46.009 --> 01:20:49.376
We can go anywhere we wanna go.
Think about that.


01:20:51.648 --> 01:20:54.742
No no no,
it started off about money,


01:20:54.785 --> 01:20:57.345
but now, l mean,


01:20:57.387 --> 01:20:59.150
honey,
everything's changed.


01:20:59.189 --> 01:21:02.317
l would hate for you


01:21:02.359 --> 01:21:05.726
to see four months


01:21:05.762 --> 01:21:08.560
of wasted time
and effort.


01:21:08.599 --> 01:21:10.533
l would really hate it.


01:21:10.567 --> 01:21:11.761
lt would hurt me.


01:21:11.802 --> 01:21:13.793
Yeah, that's what
l'm saying.


01:21:13.837 --> 01:21:15.998
So you and l, we could take
the money together.


01:21:16.039 --> 01:21:19.975
Right here.


01:21:20.010 --> 01:21:22.171
And it could happen
just with the push of a little button.


01:21:22.212 --> 01:21:24.043
We can go
anywhere we want to.


01:21:24.081 --> 01:21:26.982
We can be anybody
we want to.


01:21:27.017 --> 01:21:28.882
Think about it.


01:21:28.919 --> 01:21:32.821
Baby, that sounds
pretty fantastic.


01:21:32.856 --> 01:21:34.721
You...


01:21:34.758 --> 01:21:36.953
always told me
l was priceless.


01:21:36.994 --> 01:21:39.929
Baby, you are priceless...


01:21:39.963 --> 01:21:41.794
to me.


01:21:41.832 --> 01:21:44.198
Just didn't know


01:21:44.234 --> 01:21:46.498
that l was
a $10 million catch!


01:21:46.537 --> 01:21:48.698
- No!
- ( thud )


01:21:48.739 --> 01:21:51.207
( laughs )


01:21:51.241 --> 01:21:53.232
Mary.


01:21:54.778 --> 01:21:57.747
See now, l'm gonna have
to break up with you.


01:21:57.781 --> 01:21:59.214
For real!


01:22:02.219 --> 01:22:04.915
- ( gasps )
- ( grunting )


01:22:06.223 --> 01:22:08.214
Mare!


01:22:10.294 --> 01:22:13.525
- ( gasps )
- ( thud )


01:22:18.535 --> 01:22:20.765
Mary.
Mary, don't move.


01:22:20.804 --> 01:22:22.499
Stay right there!
Don't move.


01:22:22.539 --> 01:22:25.030
l'm gonna come to you.
You're okay.


01:22:25.075 --> 01:22:27.066
Stay right there.


01:22:49.800 --> 01:22:51.791
Okay.


01:22:53.103 --> 01:22:55.071
( crying )


01:22:55.105 --> 01:22:57.096
l'm sorry.


01:22:59.409 --> 01:23:01.400
Thank you.


01:23:22.266 --> 01:23:25.497
( siren wailing )


01:23:41.618 --> 01:23:44.018
- Detective Franklin.
- Mm-hmm.


01:23:44.054 --> 01:23:47.820
Before we go up there


01:23:47.858 --> 01:23:50.224
and see all those people,


01:23:50.260 --> 01:23:52.592
l just wanted to ask,


01:23:52.629 --> 01:23:54.620
why did you believe me?


01:23:57.968 --> 01:24:00.368
This.


01:24:00.404 --> 01:24:02.497
You left it in the chapel.


01:24:02.539 --> 01:24:04.200
What about this?


01:24:04.241 --> 01:24:06.709
The last chapter.
Take a look.


01:24:12.983 --> 01:24:15.679
The whole thing,
it's right there.


01:24:29.366 --> 01:24:32.494
Couldn't even come up
with something original.


01:24:35.138 --> 01:24:38.266
Why don't you keep this
for evidence?


01:24:38.308 --> 01:24:41.835
- You gonna be okay?
- Sure l am.


01:24:41.878 --> 01:24:44.711
Gonna just keep on living


01:24:44.748 --> 01:24:46.978
one day at a time.


01:24:47.017 --> 01:24:50.248
- How about you?
- l called my wife.


01:24:50.287 --> 01:24:53.017
- You did?
- You got me thinking.


01:24:53.056 --> 01:24:55.923
Maybe l let her go
too easily.


01:24:55.959 --> 01:24:59.395
l am proud of you, kid.
( clicks tongue )


01:24:59.429 --> 01:25:02.023
Come on. Let's get you
to a real hospital.


01:25:02.065 --> 01:25:06.001
- Okay?
- Then the games can really begin.


01:25:31.828 --> 01:25:34.763
( dramatic score playing )

